Title: Hail, Ergamenes
Order: 15
Production Code: 1x15

INT. TELASSAR - TERRACE - DAY

AMB: fountains, birdsong, a city stirring below

[[Ai]] shows [[Reuel Briggs]] the hidden city from its highest terrace — an outer and inner city built into a horseshoe curve of mountain, fields and vineyards stretching beyond.

AI
Six thousand years before Christ's birth, this city had already reached its height. Your modern world, I'm told, is still catching up to it in most things that matter.

They descend by palanquin into the city itself, drawn toward a great temple by the sound of a deep bell and a gathering crowd.

INT. TELASSAR - TEMPLE - CONTINUOUS

AMB: stringed instruments, a hush of anticipation

Inside, Council members prostrate themselves before Reuel one by one. Ai, now robed in ceremonial azure, lifts a jeweled crown — its center stone the black diamond of Senechus — and sets it on Reuel's head.

A curtain parts. Reuel finds himself alone on a platform above a vast, packed auditorium, an arch of fire overhead spelling out a single word.

CROWD (V.O.)
(as one, thunderous)
HAIL, ERGAMENES!

REUEL BRIGGS
(stunned, to Ai afterward)
Who is Ergamenes?

AI
Thou art Ergamenes — the long-looked-for king of Ethiopia, for whose reception this city was built.

At the feast that follows, musicians kneel and sing the history of the fallen dynasty Reuel is meant to restore — and, alone in the small hours with Ai, he finally understands the birthmark he has carried, unexplained, his entire life.

REUEL BRIGGS
I have carefully hidden my Ethiopian blood from the whole world, Ai. It was only ever a tradition among people who knew me as a boy — that I came from a line of African kings.

AI
Then you have come home to find out how true it was.
